From 1037a63b6e8da042f31f62ae1e2950908beeef06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dam1n19 <dam1n19@soton.ac.uk>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 08:02:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(TL-027): wire a2l _1/_3/_5 replay nodes to fixed
 local_overrides in FPGA+ASIC flists

The a2l CDC self-latch fix (WlinkGenericFCReplayV2_{1,3,5}.v, committed 9210dc5)
was shipping as a SILENT NO-OP: tidelink_fpga_v2.flist and tidelink_top_full_asic_v2.flist
still pointed the AW(_1)/W(_3)/B(_5) write-path nodes at the unfixed deps/ copies.
Re-point deps -> src/rtl/local_overrides for all three, on both FPGA and ASIC flists.

Sim-proven non-vacuous: deps FAIL (a2l_full=1/app_ready=0 ACK-lap-ahead self-latch) ->
override PASS (a2l_full=0/app_ready=1) on all 3 nodes; now gated
(sim_gate_a2l_replay_cdc_{1,3,5}). Batch sim_gate green with the re-point
(asic_v2_elab PASS, no regression).

ASIC caveat: the tapeout consumes a GENERATED flist, so this source edit is inert
until the tapeout owner regenerates it. The FPGA build picks it up directly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
